  "discussion": "Surf along north and west-facing shores will continue to decrease through today as the current small north-northwest swell fades and shifts more northerly. A more significant moderate, long- period northwest swell will arrive tonight into Thursday morning and will easily push north and west shore surf to advisory levels for Thursday into Friday. An additional medium-period moderate swell is expected to fill in on Saturday, likely prolonging moderate to large surf action into the weekend. Surf along south facing shores will remain below average today, but should see a small boost Thursday into Friday out of the south- southwest. East-facing shores will remain elevated and choppy through much of the week with the strong trades.",
